  "taper_trap": {
    "what": "`taper` flares X and Z together, so a tapered box whose X or Z reach lands on a meeting face (1.495 inset, or the 1.5 cell face) does not actually meet its neighbour - the flare pulls its far end away and opens a notch in a run that is meant to be continuous.",
    "offenders": [
      {
        "piece": "kit_brick_facade_c",
        "box": 3,
        "axis": "x",
        "reach_m": 1.495,
        "taper": [
          1.0,
          0.72
        ]
      }
    ],
    "not_fixed_here": "the one offender is kit_brick_facade_c's string course. It is pre-existing, it is brick, and brick is on this delivery's do-not-touch list. Reported so it is a known finding rather than a silent one; it costs one number to fix whenever brick is next opened.",
    "why_it_prints_instead_of_failing": "a gate that fails on a piece you are forbidden to fix is a gate that gets disabled."
  },
